WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
I also want to congratulate
you on the movie

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:07.820
Eurovision Song Contest:
The Story of Fire Saga.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.510
I watched this last night.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.450
Another enjoyable romp.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.130
I have to tell you I really enjoyed it,

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.270
but I didn't know
anything about Eurovision.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.060
The Eurovision song
contest is a real thing

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.450
that you've been obsessed
with for a while.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.660
Is that right?

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.660
Yes, it is a, it's been
going on for 60 plus years

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.920
and every year it's watched from anywhere

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
to 180 to 200 million people,

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:40.270
and it is one of the craziest
things you'll ever see.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.810
I, I discovered it literally
20 years ago with my wife.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.530
We were visiting her family in Sweden

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.140
and we, we, we had had
dinner and all of a sudden

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.323
her cousin was like, so
shall we watch Eurovision?

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.470
And I was like, okay, yeah, what's that?

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:03.470
And, and sat there for
three hours mesmerized by,

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.543
I had no idea what was going on.

00:01:07.595 --> 00:01:12.595
It is like Cirque de Soleil
meets American Idol meets,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.430
I don't know, a residency show in Vegas.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.660
It's, it's the craziest
thing you've ever seen.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.660
Also meets the Olympics because
it's different countries

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.480
going up against each
other, and one of the things

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:32.470
you capture in this movie
is there is something about

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:37.470
European entertainment
that is a very specific,

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.870
and so you, in the movie
you portray people singing

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:47.340
like rock power ballads
dressed as Vikings.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.420
That's something that really
could happen on Eurovision.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.810
100% and it's, it's so
foreign to us as Americans.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:59.540
You know, we, any sort of
our competitive music shows,

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.080
we're, we're, we're pretty much

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.323
into looking as cool as we can.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.800
In Eurovision it's quite the opposite,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.030
even though they fully
believe they're looking

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.400
as cool as possible, but
yeah, you'll, you'll see

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.400
everything from costumes,
a lot of pyrotechnics,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.490
a lot of people just onstage doing nothing

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.315
that has anything to do with the song,

00:02:24.315 --> 00:02:25.440
(chuckling)

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.170
including one of the, I've actually been

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.710
to three of them in
person, and one of the bits

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.690
that we actually lifted
and put in the movie

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.840
was I think, I believe it was the Ukraine

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.040
and this, this singer was, was singing,

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.500
but behind them on the stage was a man

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.090
just running in a life,
human sized hamster wheel

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.890
for three minutes and was never
referenced in any way and.

00:02:54.361 --> 00:02:55.900
Had nothing to do with the song.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.150
Nothing to do with the song.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.910
The singer didn't look back.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:03.040
The, they even got a tight shot of the guy

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.300
running in a hamster wheel
and he just kept running.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.022
He wouldn't even look at the camera.

00:03:07.022 --> 00:03:10.321
♪ My heart is like a clock,
I'm steady like a rock ♪

00:03:10.321 --> 00:03:14.510
♪ Shh, don't stop, kiss
and kiss me till I drop ♪

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.587
♪ My heart is like a clock,
you wind it with your love ♪

00:03:17.587 --> 00:03:19.630
And we were obsessed
with that image that we,

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.440
we ended up putting it in the movie.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.070
You know, what I love is that
you're in the hamster wheel

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:29.070
running full out, but unlike
the example you just gave,

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.980
you also have to sing while you're running

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.930
full out in the hamster wheel.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.613
Looks hilarious and I imagine
was next to impossible.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.810
Well, it is one of those moments where,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:47.160
and I've found myself on numerous
occasions over my career,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.000
when I read something on the page,

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.419
I forget that I'm actually
going to have to do it,

00:03:51.419 --> 00:03:53.190
(chuckling)

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:58.190
and there I was on that day
being hoisted about 50 feet

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:03.210
above the ground in a hamster
wheel that I kind of had to

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:07.193
control with my own gait
and then singing the lyrics,

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.860
but you know, we got it done.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.490
You got it done.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.783
You got it done in style.

00:04:17.162 --> 00:04:21.360
But the, but the prop master did remind me

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.850
on several occasions how difficult it was

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.681
to build that hamster wheel.

00:04:25.681 --> 00:04:27.270
(snickering)

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:29.280
I was like, okay, but isn't that your job?

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.400
Yeah, but I'm just telling you there's 97,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:35.263
there's 96 weld joints alone
on that piece of steel.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.200
All right.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.700
Okay, thank you.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.720
Yeah, thank you.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.540
I think he was looking
for a big thank you.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.548
Thank you. I said thank you.

00:04:44.548 --> 00:04:46.430
I could have said thank you more.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.233
I should've sent him Omaha steaks.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:55.220
You, you reveal that you have
quite a nice singing voice,

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.650
Will, and I, it leads me
to wonder what about you

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.140
putting out an album, Will Ferrell Sings?

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.903
Is that something that could happen?

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.530
You know, it could, you never
know, but I would probably

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.750
be drawn to more of a spoken word album.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.500
I'd love to bring back spoken word.

00:05:19.017 --> 00:05:21.100
You mean, just saying the lyrics.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.600
Saying the lyrics.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.020
Not actually singing the song.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:28.610
Nope, and not like eight or 10 songs,

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.683
30 to 50 songs spoken word.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.650
That's going to be a
very, very long album.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.800
You're going to, you're
going to want to sit back

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.550
and really, really be able to dedicate

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.060
a nice chunk of time to it.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.840
Yeah, I think you're
gonna want to listen to it

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.543
as you drive from L.A. to Boston,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.370
and you're going to maybe
just get through all the songs

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.670
maybe as you get to Framingham, Mass.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:54.503
Exactly.

00:05:54.503 --> 00:05:57.530
In fact, I'm going to, that's
how I'm going to do a dry run

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.623
where I time it, so when
you pull into Framingham,

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.000
you finished the album.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.540
Okay. This sounds like a awful idea.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.373
Thank you.

00:06:08.373 --> 00:06:09.710
You've given me a great idea.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:10.680
No, don't do it.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.836
Wait, what'd you say?

00:06:11.836 --> 00:06:13.996
Don't do it. It's a bad idea.

00:06:13.996 --> 00:06:14.829
Got it.

00:06:14.829 --> 00:06:16.270
No. (snickers)

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.230
Got it.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.810
No. There's a scene in
the movie, you know, I.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:21.643
No, no.

00:06:21.643 --> 00:06:23.680
Don't, don't make your spoken word album.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.100
No, no salute.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.960
No, no one has ever saluted.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.255
Thank you. Conan.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:30.360
(laughing)

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.683
Such a bad idea.

